# Copy to /etc/yijianjifa-cloud-voice/service.env, owned by root, mode 0600.
# systemd reads this file. Never put it in Git, a web root or shell history.
YJJF_CLOUD_DATABASE=/var/lib/yijianjifa-cloud-voice/voice.db
SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt

# Account/credit/redemption-only stage: leave ALL supplier options absent.
# It will return service_not_configured for voices and generation.
# Later, securely choose ONE authentication method:
# New console: YJJF_VOLC_API_KEY
# Legacy console: YJJF_VOLC_APP_ID AND YJJF_VOLC_ACCESS_KEY (Access Token)
# Never mix the two methods; do not substitute general IAM AK/SK.
# Both methods also require the two common settings:
# YJJF_CLOUD_VOICES_FILE (absolute path to an approved JSON voice list)
# YJJF_CLOUD_MAX_DAILY_WORDS (positive integer daily submission limit)
# Do not copy any credentials from existing apps or inherited environments.

# Optional legacy audio directory: new direct-download jobs do not store audio.
# YJJF_CLOUD_AUDIO_DIR (absolute path; leave absent for this new installation)
# Internal loopback stage has no reverse proxy: leave trusted proxies absent.
# YJJF_CLOUD_TRUSTED_PROXIES (only after HTTPS proxy setup and X-Real-IP overwrite)
